.TH ED 1 "FUZIX" "Ripple"
.SH NAME
ed \- edit text by line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
ed [file]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Ed accepts line-oriented editing commands. a appends text, i inserts text,
and c replaces lines. End text entry with a line containing only a dot.
p prints addressed lines; 1,$p prints the whole buffer. w writes the
buffer, and w filename writes to a named file.
.PP
q quits when no unsaved changes remain. Q quits and discards changes.
Ctrl-C interrupts the editor and returns to the shell.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ed note
a
hello Ripple
.
w
q
.fi
